  body: "# Suspension of benefit payment in the DMG\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe guidance describes withholding
    all or part of payment while specified questions about entitlement, revision, supersession, appeals or information
    are considered.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nPayment suspension is not equated with termination or a final
    entitlement decision. The source requires attention to hardship and contains benefit-specific provisions; an
    unanswered request does not justify an automatic project decision.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG
    04800, PDF page 121](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a105e7a1eb143220d8d27f1/dmg-ch-04.pdf#page=121)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 4: Supersession, suspension and termination .\n- [DMG 04810, PDF page 122](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a105e7a1eb143220d8d27f1/dmg-ch-04.pdf#page=122)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 4: Supersession, suspension and termination .\n- [DMG 04811, PDF page 122](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a105e7a1eb143220d8d27f1/dmg-ch-04.pdf#page=122)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 4: Supersession, suspension and termination .\n- [DMG 04841, PDF page 126](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a105e7a1eb143220d8d27f1/dmg-ch-04.pdf#page=126)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 4: Supersession, suspension and termination .\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted
    interpretation of the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source
    is DWP guidance, not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication,
    not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are
    one-based file positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships
    preserve extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current
    applicability remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol1-ch4` PDF SHA-256: `9c96b49a78aa4dc40df8594cf65cbd435a681d0be3737729cd87882542d0e2ea`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `bef5fc9f04b2a78c5bb5dc99468f94a1841f1ef4afa117d47aa9c1e5040f3752`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-revision
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: One described ground for considering suspension is a question whether an award should be
      revised; the relation records a possibility, not a mandatory result.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch4/0122
      quote: "04811 Suspension may be appropriate where a question has arisen during the currency of a claim\n\n\
        \n1. about whether the claimant satisfies the conditions of entitlement to the benefit 1\n\n\n2. about whether
        an award of benefit should be revised or superseded 2\n\n\n3. about the award of benefit because an appeal
        is pending against a decision made by a FtT, UT or a\n\ncourt3\n\n\n4. because an appeal is pending in a
        different case before a UT or a court, and it appears to the DM that\n\nthe outcome of that case might require
        the award to be revised or superseded 4\n\n\n5. about whether an overpayment of benefit is recoverable 5\n\
        \n\n6. about whether the claimant is still residing at the last address notified to the Secretary of State
        6.\n\n\n             1 SS CS (D&A) Regs, reg 16(3)(a)(i); 2 reg 16(3)(a)(ii); 3 SS Act 98, s 21(2)(c); SS
        CS (D&A) Regs,\n                                 reg 16(3)(b) & (4); 4 SS Act 98, s 21(2)(d); SS CS (D&A)
        Regs, reg 16 (3)(b)(i);\n                                  5 SS Act 98, s 21(1)(a); SS CS (D&A) Regs, reg
        16(3)(a)(iii); 6 reg 16(3)(a)(iv)"
      locator: DMG 04811
